@@ -1,5 +1,13 @@
 ## Unreleased — Meta AI Developer Hackathon 2026
 
+- Add `doc timelines "<task>" --test "<command>"`, parallel timelines part 1 (everything but Wonder's judging).
+  - The base is a dmc export of the latest closed checkpoint's after-state, or `--from <cp> --state before|after`; the working copy is never read.
+  - Muse Wonder (`planner` role) plans exactly N (`--n`, default 3) clearly different approaches as validated JSON (`response_format` schema, strict parsing, one retry), from the task, the matched lesson brief, the base checkpoint's label and changed files and a redacted file list.
+  - After one confirmation with a stated cost estimate, each approach gets a Git worktree under Doc's data dir (outside the repository) whose tree is exactly the base, committed as "timeline base: <cp> <state>", with its own dmc vault.
+  - N `muse exec` agents run in parallel with Muse Code's default approval and sandbox, `--max-model-steps`, `--disable-web-tools` and `--json`, a per-timeline timeout and status lines; Ctrl-C stops them all and keeps the worktrees.
+  - Each result is committed on `doc/timeline/<run>/<k>`, tested with bisect's runner (`--setup`, `--link`), and compared side by side (steps, time, cost from Muse's `run.usage`, files with +/− lines, tests). The run is saved as JSON (`--json`).
+  - `doc timelines pick` shows the diff and prints the git commands (patch + `git apply --3way`, or `git merge --no-ff`) and runs nothing in the repository; the others stay as archived branches. `list`, `show` and `clean` (worktree folders only, never branches). `--local` refuses it.
+- Move bisect's shell runner, output tail and `--link` handling into a shared probe runner (no behaviour change).
 - Add `doc talk` (alias `doc hey`), "Hey Doc" push-to-talk with Muse Voice Transcribe. Nothing is recorded or sent until Space or Enter; the same key (or 30 seconds) stops, Esc cancels and sends nothing more, and the terminal is always restored. Audio is recorded with `rec` (SoX) or `ffmpeg` (AVFoundation) and streamed by Doc alone over Meta's realtime WebSocket as documented: the key in the handshake frame, 80 ms binary PCM16 frames paced in real time, `{"type":"endStream"}`, then `transcript` events (cumulative partials, then `final: true`). `--file <audio>` streams a recording at real-time pace (converted with sox or ffmpeg when needed). Recent file names are sent as recognition `keywords`.
   - The redacted transcript is classified by the workhorse role as JSON (`response_format` schema, strict parsing, one retry), and `planVoiceAction` (pure) turns it into one Doc command: restore (the transcript goes to natural-language restore unchanged), summarize the latest checkpoint, lesson brief, lessons, bisect (test command from the per-workspace `bisectTest` config or asked for) or status. Doc asks "Run it? [y/N]" and runs the command in-process only on yes; `--yes` never answers it for restore or bisect. Unknown or low-confidence requests run nothing.
   - `--local` refuses `doc talk`. Usage records billed audio seconds; the price is configurable per model (default $0.18 per hour, Meta's pricing page).
